(d) lateral and oppositely lateral “C” brackets respectively opening at the trolley's lateral and oppositely lateral sides;

(e) a jack screw assembly comprising a helically threaded shaft, said assembly being connected operatively to the trolley for alternatively longitudinally and oppositely longitudinally moving the trolley;

(f) lateral and oppositely lateral tracks having longitudinally extending edges and respectively supporting the lateral and oppositely lateral rollers, each of the “C” brackets' openings receiving one of the longitudinally extending edges;

(g) a scissor arm matrix having a lower end connected operatively to the trolley;

(h) a load platform connected operatively to an upper end of the scissor arm matrix; and

(i) turning means connected operatively to the jack screw assembly for actuating the trolley's alternative longitudinal and oppositely longitudinal movements and for alternatively lowering and raising the scissor arm matrix and load platform.

